From e574328aca1a4972c0807f2131ae1151d4c75e54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yuhangle <893033655@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 14:34:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] zram: backport compression backends API, dictionary support,
 LZ4 template stream

Backport of the upstream zram compression backends series (merged for
v6.14, 2024-09-02, Sergey Senozhatsky) plus the LZ4 dictionary template
stream optimization (upstream commit f0f6f7871430, gao xu).

- zcomp: replace the crypto compress API with in-kernel per-algorithm
  backends: lzo, lzo-rle, lz4, lz4hc, zstd, deflate and 842
- introduce struct zcomp_params (level, dict, deflate.winbits) which is
  owned by zram and shared by all streams of a device
- add write-only /sys/block/zram<id>/algorithm_params knob, accepting
  level=<n>, dict=<path> and deflate.winbits=<n>; parameters can only be
  set before the device is initialized
- keep the 6.1 single compression stream layout and per-CPU local_lock
  stream model (no multi-comp, no per-priority param slots)
- lz4 backend: build the dictionary stream once in setup_params() and
  memcpy that template into the per-CPU stream on each compression,
  instead of calling LZ4_loadDict() for every request
- lib/lz4: export LZ4_compress_fast_continue and LZ4_resetStreamHC (zram
  is built as a module), define LZ4_ACCELERATION_DEFAULT for the kernel
  <linux/lz4.h> wrapper
- gki_defconfig: enable the lzo, lz4, lz4hc, zstd, deflate and 842
  backends, default compressor stays lzo-rle
---
