diff --git a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-block-zram b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-block-zram
index 14b2bf2e5105..09c67bfcd883 100644
--- a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-block-zram
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-block-zram
@@ -137,3 +137,26 @@ Description:
 		The writeback_limit file is read-write and specifies the maximum
 		amount of writeback ZRAM can do. The limit could be changed
 		in run time.
+
+What:		/sys/block/zram<id>/algorithm_params
+Date:		August 2024
+Contact:	Sergey Senozhatsky <senozhatsky@chromium.org>
+Description:
+		The algorithm_params file is write-only and is used to setup
+		compression algorithm parameters.  The following parameters
+		are supported:
+
+		level=<int>
+			Compression level.  Meaning depends on the algorithm
+			(zstd compression level, deflate compression level,
+			lz4 acceleration, lz4hc compression level).
+
+		dict=<path>
+			Path to the compression dictionary.  Supported by the
+			lz4, lz4hc and zstd backends.
+
+		deflate.winbits=<int>
+			Window bits for the deflate backend.
+
+		Parameters can only be changed before the device is
+		initialized (disksize is set).
